<div class="player-stat-label">Wingspan — 1,679th all time</div>
</div>
<div class="player-stat above">
<div class="player-stat-val">~33</div>
<div class="player-stat-label">2026 Finals PPG</div>
</div>
<div class="player-stat above">
<div class="player-stat-val">MVP</div>
<div class="player-stat-label">2026 Finals MVP</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Brunson finishes the 2026 Finals averaging approximately 33 points per game across five games, anchoring an offense that needed to play through the Defensive Player of the Year on every single possession. His Game 4 performance — 36 points and the largest comeback in Finals history — looked like it might be the signature moment of the series. Then, with a championship on the line in Game 5, he topped it: 45 points, 3 rebounds, and 3 assists on the road to close it out. The Finals MVP award reflects the totality of the run — clutch shot-making in Games 1 and 2, finding his shot at Madison Square Garden in Game 3, the historic comeback in Game 4, and a 45-point closeout for the championship in Game 5. The same wingspan that ranked 1,679th out of 1,812 players ever tested is now attached to a championship ring and a Finals MVP trophy.</p>
<div class="callout">
<div class="callout-icon">🏀</div>
<div class="callout-text"><strong>The Tom Brady parallel, completed:</strong> Tom Brady's <a href="/relative-athletic-score-nfl">Relative Athletic Score</a> of approximately 1.0 out of 10 did not stop him from winning seven Super Bowls. Brunson's combine profile — bottom 7 to 11 percent across height, wingspan, and standing reach — just produced an NBA championship and a Finals MVP. Both players were measured accurately. Both tests correctly identified real physical limitations. And in both cases, the things that actually determine greatness — processing speed, decision-making, footwork, competitive will — were sitting outside the testing booth the entire time.</div>
</div>
<h2>Brunson vs Wembanyama — Final Tale of the Tape</h2>
<p>The final tale of the tape between the Finals' two central figures remains as lopsided as it was on day one — and the scoreboard tells the opposite story.</p>
<div class="table-scroll"><table class="data-table">
<thead>
<tr>
