<h2>Brunson Joins the Shortest Finals MVPs in NBA History</h2>
<p>At 6 feet 1 inch barefoot, Brunson is now among the shortest players to ever win Finals MVP, joining a list that includes Isiah Thomas (6'1", two championships with Detroit) and the broader company of undersized guards — Allen Iverson, Tony Parker, Steph Curry — who reached the same stage at similar height but with dramatically different wingspans.</p>
<p>What separates Brunson from nearly everyone on that list is the wingspan gap. Curry's wingspan is only an inch longer than his height — close to Brunson's 3-inch differential, but Curry's game is built around a release so quick and a range so deep that length matters less. Brunson's game is built on contact, change of speed, and an almost supernatural ability to get to a spot a half-step before the defense recovers. Different tools, same conclusion: the combine measured the wrong things.</p>
